// Starship (full stack) - two-stage methalox super-heavy-lift vehicle.
//
// Simplification: booster and ship are sequential stages; the booster keeps
// the real 3-center / 10-mid-ring / 20-outer-ring Raptor layout at
// representative stage-local stations. Sea-level Raptors are rated at sea
// level; RVacs are rated in vacuum. Ambient back-pressure is handled by ISP
// blending in the simulator.
//
// FAA source: SpaceX Starship/Super Heavy operational envelope (July 2025),
// https://www.faa.gov/space/stakeholder_resources/environmental/spacex_starship
// Sources (rough public figures): SpaceX Starship updates - Super Heavy
// ~71 m Super Heavy / ~50 m Ship; ~200 t dry / ~3 400 t propellant, 33 Raptors x ~2 256 kN SL (~7 500 tf
// liftoff); Ship ~110 t dry / ~1 200 t propellant, 3 sea-level + 3 vacuum
// Raptors; Raptor ISP ~327 s (SL) / ~350 s (vac), RVac ~372 s; deep throttle
// to about 40 percent. No payload fairing: payload bay door instead.
// Ignition budgets are conservative catalog assumptions for this simulator,
// not source-verified operational limits.

